💳 Simple Banking App
Welcome to my Simple Banking App, a small Java project that simulates basic banking operations like deposits, withdrawals, and balance checks. It's entirely run in the console and was built to help me practice object-oriented programming and user interaction in Java.

🛠️ This is my second solo coding project — it's a work in progress and I'm learning as I go!

🚀 Features
- Create and store multiple user accounts

- Login simulation via name matching

- Deposit money into your account

- Withdraw money (with validation to prevent overdraft)

- View current account balance

- Console-based menu and interaction


📂 Project Structure
- BankingApp.java – base class with deposit and withdrawal methods

- BankUser.java – extends BankingApp, adds user-specific info (name and balance)

- Main.java – the main class that handles user interaction through the console


✅ Option 1: Using IntelliJ IDEA

1. Open the project in IntelliJ.

2. Locate Main.java inside the src folder.

3. Right-click on Main.java → Run 'Main'.

4. The program will launch in the terminal at the bottom of the window.

✅ Option 2: Using the Command Line

1. Open your terminal and navigate to the src/ directory:
cd C:\Users\aless\JavaProjects\SimpleBankingApp\SimpleBankingApp/src

2. Compile the Java files:
javac Main.java BankUser.java BankingApp.java

3. Run the program:
java Main

⚠️ Make sure you're inside the src/ directory when running these commands, since there are no packages used.

👨‍💼 Sample Interaction:
Hello and welcome! Please enter your first name:
> Alessio
Thank you! Now please enter your last name:
> Scarpello
Match Found!
Welcome Alessio Scarpello!
What would you like to do? Press D for deposit, W to withdraw, B to show your balance, or Q to exit:
> B
Hello Alessio, here's your balance left: £2458.24


🧠 What I Learned
- How to use classes and inheritance in Java

- Validating user input

- Managing lists of objects (ArrayList)

- Handling console interaction with Scanner

